{
  "$schema": "https://kinetixui.com/schema/components-manifest.json",
  "$description": "The single source of truth for per-component metadata. `pnpm gen:manifest` derives component-status.json and platform-parity.json from this file — edit HERE, never those. Every component in packages/ui has an entry (enforced by `pnpm check:manifest`). status: \"beta\" | \"stable\" | \"deprecated\" — a new component ships \"beta\" for the release cycle it lands in (\"beta\" means new, not incomplete), then flips to \"stable\"; nothing is deprecated yet. platforms: every platform the component ships on, explicitly. Where a component is intentionally not on a platform, `platformNote` says why (visual parity is not the goal — token parity plus behavioural-intent parity plus a platform-native implementation is). Regenerate the platform port list by diffing slugs against packages/ui-compose/ui/src/main/kotlin/com/kinetixui/ui/*.kt (PascalCase), packages/ui-swiftui/Sources/KinetixUI/*.swift (PascalCase) and packages/ui-flutter/lib/src/*.dart (snake_case); `sonner` resolves to Sonner/Toaster/toaster. `registry: false` marks a docs-page component that ships inside another component's registry item (avatar-group in avatar, combobox in multi-select) rather than as its own.",
  "platforms": [
    "React",
    "SwiftUI",
    "Compose",
    "Flutter"
  ],
  "nativePlatforms": [
    "SwiftUI",
    "Compose",
    "Flutter"
  ],
  "platformAbbr": {
    "React": "RE",
    "SwiftUI": "SW",
    "Compose": "JC",
    "Flutter": "FL"
  },
